  "database": "rschema_0121",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0121 database is designed to manage user authentication, services, and their interactions. At its core, the database contains a table called 'user' which stores information about each registered user, including their unique identifier, username, full name, email, password hash, registration date, and last login date. Each user can be associated with an 'authenticated_user' table, which tracks their authentication level, signature, issuer, and authentication time. The 'service' table stores details about the services available, including their unique identifier, name, type, URL, configuration data, last heartbeat time, monitoring status, signature, and issuer. Worker nodes, which are essentially machines that run these services, are stored in the 'worker_node' table, which includes their unique identifier, name, status, service ID, operating system, architecture, last heartbeat time, signature, and issuer. The 'authenticated_consumer' table links users to their associated consumers, which are essentially applications or entities that use these services, and includes information such as the consumer's ID, user ID, name, description, type, configuration data, permissions, signature, and issuer. The 'user_migration' table tracks user ID changes over time, including the old and new user IDs, migration time, and a unique migration ID. Sessions, which are essentially temporary connections between consumers and services, are stored in the 'session' table, which includes the session ID, consumer ID, expiration time, MFA status, signature, and issuer. Finally, the 'encrypted_data_test' table stores sensitive data, including regular data, sensitive data 1 and 2, signature, and issuer, with a unique data ID. Throughout the database, foreign keys are used to establish relationships between tables, such as the 'authenticated_user' table referencing the 'user' table, and the 'session' table referencing the 'authenticated_consumer' table, with cascade delete and update rules applied to ensure data consistency.",
  "gold_question": "User Authentication and Management System\nThis system is designed to manage and authenticate users while tracking their interactions with various services and worker nodes in the system. The key functionalities of the system are:\n1.User Registration and Management:\nStore user registration information, including username, full name, email, password hash, registration date, and last login date.\nEnsure the uniqueness of usernames and email addresses.\n2.User Authentication:\nStore information of authenticated users, including username, full name, authentication level (ring), and authentication time.\nEnsure the uniqueness of authenticated usernames.\nRecord signatures and issuer information during the authentication process.\n3.User Migration:\nTrack user migrations from an old system to the new system, recording the old and new user IDs, along with the migration time.\n4.Authenticated Consumer Management:\nStore information of authenticated consumers, including name, description, type, and associated user ID.\nStore configuration data,permissions, and signatures for each consumer.\n5.Session Management:\nStore session information, including session ID, associated consumer ID, expiration time, and MFA (Multi-Factor Authentication) status.\nRecord session signatures and issuer information.\n6.Service Management:\nStore information of various services in the system, including service name, type, URL, and configuration.\nTrack the last heartbeat time and monitoring status of services.\nRecord service signatures and issuer information.\n7.Worker Node Management:\nStore information of worker nodes, including node name, status, associated service ID, operating system, architecture, and last heartbeat time.\nRecord worker node signatures and issuer information.\nEach service contains multiple worker nodes, each user may have multiple authenticated consumers, and each consumer will have multiple sessions.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0121.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0121\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `full_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password_hash` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_login_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `authenticated_user` (\n  `auth_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `auth_level` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `signature` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `issuer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `auth_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`auth_user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `authenticated_user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `service` (\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `config_data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_heartbeat_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `monitoring_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `signature` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `issuer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`service_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `worker_node` (\n  `worker_node_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operating_system` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `architecture` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_heartbeat_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `signature` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `issuer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`worker_node_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `worker_node_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `service` (`service_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `authenticated_consumer` (\n  `consumer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `config_data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `permissions` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `signature` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `issuer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`consumer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `authenticated_consumer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_migration` (\n  `migration_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `old_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `new_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `migration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`migration_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `session` (\n  `session_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `consumer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `mfa_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `signature` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `issuer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`session_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `session_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`consumer_id`) REFERENCES `authenticated_consumer` (`consumer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `encrypted_data_test` (\n  `data_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `regular_data` text NOT NULL,\n  `sensitive_data_1` text NOT NULL,\n  `sensitive_data_2` text NOT NULL,\n  `signature` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `issuer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`data_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
